            ("When is a tendon graft needed instead of direct repair?", "When the tendon ends cannot be brought together without excessive tension, often because of delay, tissue loss or previous failed repair. A graft bridges the gap, sometimes in two planned stages. Dr Reddy explains at consultation whether your injury suits direct repair or grafting."),
            ("My injury is months old. Is it too late?", "Not necessarily, though the surgery becomes more involved. Old tendon injuries can often be reconstructed with grafts or tendon transfers, where a neighbouring tendon is rerouted to restore the lost movement. Assessment will show what remains possible, and honest counselling follows."),
